    "description": "Pattern Energy Group LP is a San Francisco-headquartered developer, owner, and operator of utility-scale wind, solar, energy storage, and transmission infrastructure across North America. The company reports 46 operating facilities totaling approximately 12 GW and a 40 GW development and active-construction portfolio. CPP Investments has owned the platform since the March 2020 take-private and holds 69.1% after Pattern completed its share-based acquisition of CPP-owned Cordelio Power on April 2, 2026. On June 9, 2025, an APG- and ART-headed consortium that also included a CalSTRS buyer vehicle acquired Riverstone's entire stake alongside Pattern management; the individual consortium and management stakes were not disclosed. Riverstone had backed Pattern since its 2009 formation and rolled its interest through the 2020 combination before exiting in 2025.",
